      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's great that you are focusing on a diet rich in greens for your heart health! However, some leafy greens, like spinach and kale, contain Vitamin K, which can interact with warfarin. Too much Vitamin K can potentially reduce the effectiveness of your blood thinner, so please discuss your increased intake with your doctor or pharmacist. They can advise you on safe quantities so you can maintain your healthy eating habits without risking complications.",
